<p>I like the crow versus octopus war.</p>
<p>First the technical error:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2967 is an abnormally large specimen of cephalopod of an unidentified species, sharing most traits with <em>octopus vulgaris</em>. SCP-2967 is roughly 33cm in mantle length, with its arms stretching up to roughly 1.5m long.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That isn't abnormally large for a cephalopod species. There are at least two species of octopus with mantle lengths above 60&#160;cm (<em>Haliphron atlanticus</em> and <em>Enteroctopus dofleini</em>) dozens of squid species that are larger still (up to 3&#160;m), there are even several species of cuttlefish that are larger than your &quot;abnormally large&quot; octopus.</p>
<p>Also generic names are always capitalized so it should be &quot;<em>Octopus vulgaris</em>&quot;. Common names are lower case (except when they contain a proper noun) so &quot;common octopus&quot;. I have fixed these for you.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Kain Pathos Crow</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Some old school author avatars (the Brights and Mann for example) hold up okay nowadays, but this isn't one of them, IMO. And that whole bit at the end, seems like a throwback.</p>

							</div>

								
